  "lineage": "The Latin exorcism recitation is the imprecatory liturgy of the Roman Catholic Rituale Romanum, whose exorcism section (De exorcizandis obsessis a daemonio) was codified in 1614 and revised in 1999. Performed by a priest with the bishop's mandate, it interleaves psalmody, Gospel readings, and the imperative deprecatory-and-imperative formulae addressed directly to the demon ('Exorcizo te, immundissime spiritus'). Delivery is forceful heightened Latin declamation in a resonant church interior, punctuated by the sign of the cross and sprinkling of holy water. The rite is documented in the Rituale itself and in the Church's liturgical-law tradition.",
